while explicit child props—including disabled-state props—and\n`className` values remain available for local customization. Separator, page count,\n`Select` and\n`PaginationDots` are consumer-owned."},"1056":{"id":"/docs/components/pagination-28","page_id":"/docs/components/pagination","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pagination#customization","content":"Use `className` to extend styling without replacing the interaction behavior\nprovided by Antares."},"1057":{"id":"/docs/components/pagination-29","page_id":"/docs/components/pagination","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pagination#accessibility","content":"Pagination does not add translated labels. Provide accessible names for the\nnavigation region, previous/next buttons and page input."},"1058":{"id":"/docs/components/pagination-30","page_id":"/docs/components/pagination","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pagination#accessibility","content":"`PaginationDots` is decorative and does not replace interactive page\ncontrols."},"1059":{"id":"/docs/components/pagination-31","page_id":"/docs/components/pagination","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pagination#accessibility","content":"For interactive page links, compose explicit `Button` or `LinkButton` children and\nprovide the active state with `aria-current=\"page\"`."},"1060":{"id":"/docs/components/pagination-32","page_id":"/docs/components/pagination","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pagination#best-practices","content":"Pass `pageCount` when the backend exposes a known number of pages."},"1061":{"id":"/docs/components/pagination-33","page_id":"/docs/components/pagination","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/pagination#best-practices","content":"Omit `pageCount` for cursor-based data and disable the composed next button\nwhen the backend reports that there is no next page."},"1062":{"id":"/docs/components/pagination-34","page_id":"/docs/components/pagination","tags":[],"type":"text",